      "observations": "Reran every doneWhen in the integrated main checkout after a full turbo build, because cross-package tests resolve to dist: asset-registry and xr-runtime-state regressions 19/19, sway and composition call site 6/6, the named behavior test 4/4, assert-contract-live 1 contract live, verifier suite 22/22. Ran an own revert probe independent of the implementer eight-change sweep: reverting only packages/openclinxr/xr-runtime-state/src/supported-actor-placement.ts to dc2ad3b8 and rebuilding fails all four behavior clauses including SC-03-required-behavior, the post-acceptance replacement counterweight, the malformed-frame and GLB-scale counterweight, and the standing known-good; restoring passes 4 of 4. ACCEPTED THE IMPLEMENTER OWN DISCLOSURE RATHER THAN LETTING IT PASS QUIETLY: it implemented before running the test the first time, so its RED was measured by removing the fix rather than at the untouched baseline. The behavior test names supportAcceptance and a third actorPlacement argument, neither of which exists at dc2ad3b8, so a direct baseline run cannot compile and proof-contract-v2 sanctions the substitution; the ordering was still wrong and the report says so, which is the behaviour the contract asks for. The per-change transcript names a distinct failing clause for each of the eight reverts, so the substitution is decisive rather than a single undifferentiated red. The finding that matters most for the rest of the package is that the heading defect sits INSIDE SC-00 yaw tolerance: authored -0.26 against framing default -0.18 is 4.58 degrees against a 10 degree cap, so a run that silently dropped the authored heading would have passed settled-heading with 5.4 degrees to spare, and only a direct identity assertion catches that class. Verified no regression: 433 tests across every landed card in this package, 241 across the three touched packages, 86 in xr-runtime-state after my own repair. Ratchets verified unmoved: apps/ui-xr/src exactly 10